.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-ENC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-enc
.Nd encapsulate a shared secret to an ML-KEM or HQC public key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis enc
.Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl o Ar ct
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar ss | Fl -stdout
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis enc
runs the encapsulation of the KEM named in
.Ar key.pub
with fresh randomness.
It writes the ciphertext (raw bytes, the standard's encoding) to
.Ar ct
and the 32-byte shared secret to
.Ar ss ,
created owner-only (mode 0600).
Send
.Ar ct
to the holder of the secret key; they recover the same secret with
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
A public KEM key file
.Pq Ql noqtis-key-1 ML-KEM-768 pub , No for example .
A signature key is refused.
An HQC public key of specification 5.0 (noqtis before 0.3.0) has the
length of a 5.1 key and is not refused; the secret it gives is not one
the key's holder can recover with a 5.0 implementation.
Encapsulate only to HQC keys made by noqtis 0.3.0 or later.
.It Fl o Ar ct , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar ct
The ciphertext file (always needed, with
.Fl -stdout
too).
.It Fl -stdout
Print the shared secret in hex (64 digits and a newline) on standard
output instead of writing
.Ar ss .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace existing files.
.El
.Pp
The ciphertext and the shared secret are both written under temporary
names in their folders before either is renamed into place, the shared
secret first and the ciphertext last (with
.Fl -stdout ,
the ciphertext is renamed only once the secret is printed), so a run
that fails or is stopped never leaves a ciphertext whose shared secret
was lost.
.Pp
The shared secret is key material: feed it to a key derivation function
or an authenticated cipher; it is not a password.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on a usage error, a key that is not a public KEM key, an
existing file without
.Fl -force ,
or a file that cannot be written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-KEM-768 -o box
ML-KEM-768 key pair: box (secret), box.pub (public)
$ noqtis enc -p box.pub -o msg.ct sender.ss
$ noqtis dec -k box -o receiver.ss msg.ct
$ cmp sender.ss receiver.ss && echo same
same
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr nqenc 3
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 203 (ML-KEM), HQC version 5.1.
.Rs
.%Q National Institute of Standards and Technology
.%T Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard
.%R FIPS 203
.%D August 2024
.Re
.Rs
.%Q HQC team
.%T Hamming Quasi-Cyclic (HQC), specification, version 5.1
.%D November 9, 2026
.%U https://pqc-hqc.org/doc/hqc_specifications_v5.1.pdf
.Re
